dle that for so long  right like month after month after month  after month after trial and failing and  trial and failing and  like how do you keep going i got to the  point where i was so  down on myself so depressed so feeling  like a failure  where my whole life i had been you know  pretty successful with whatever i tried  to do  and here i was i couldn't make this  thing happen i felt defeated and i felt  like  i lost my confidence in myself and what  i was doing  and normally i my two business partners  i got along with them very well  but you can only handle so much defeat  and failure and just  not seeing any progress  and it all came to head one day  i was at a family function i was at my  mom's house i forget what it was  and i hopped on a call with my  business partner for some reason and and  we just had different visions now for  you know well we had the same vision we  had different directions where we wanted  to take it right you know we were  fighting we  i wanted to do this you want to do  something else and  you start fighting when you're not  making money  and i told them you know what i'm done i  quit you know i don't respect myself  anymore  i can't keep doing this and not making  any money i quit i'm out i'm done  and i hung up the phone angrily and  and i just cried cried like i'm  genuinely not a huge crier but i just  cried i  bawled my eyes out i was just so like  hearing myself say that i quit and  giving up on something that i believed  in  i was so i felt defeated i felt broken i  felt broken  it was a good word and uh  my mom heard me crying and she came  upstairs and and i don't even know what  she said to me  uh she put her hand on my shoulder and  it was just so  i was so lost in my tears and my pain  and tears are balling out you know  coming out of my nose it was just  one of the worst days of my life and  that's where things that's where you get  tested  you know that's where you get tested if  you're doing the right thing or not 